:name: HWA10 machine setup
:description: Everything both run scripts share: boot images, the memory patches
:  the sim needs, and the peripheral inputs. Include this, then RunFor or start.

include @scripts/boot.resc
logLevel 3

# --- known-good boot patch set ---
# The patches are generated from abi/sim.yaml by abi/rig.py, which resolves each
# site as a symbol plus an offset against the symbol table of the image this run
# loads and refuses if the bytes there are not the ones the entry expects, so a
# relinked or relaid-out image needs no rewriting step here.
# imagePatches is a macro because the bootloader rewrites internal flash from the
# external bank on an update, which takes the patches with it; the update run
# re-applies them when the freshly flashed application is entered.
include @out/rig/patches.resc
# The addresses the runs hook, from the same generator.
include @out/rig/hooks.resc
runMacro $imagePatches
# MBR + SoftDevice must come out of the run byte-identical to this point: a
# difference means a stray store that silicon would have dropped (flash is
# read-only unless NVMC WEN).
sysbus.nvmc SnapshotProtectedRegion 0x0 0x27000
# Peripheral state below is lost on SYSRESETREQ (the app's fault handler
# resets), so it lives in the machine's reset macro, which Renode re-runs then.
macro reset
"""
    # tickless idle wakes via SEVONPEND (app IRQs are NVIC-disabled inside the
    # sd_nvic critical region). Renode 1.17's NVIC checks the wrong security
    # bank of SCR.SEVONPEND on non-TrustZone cores, so write the bank it reads.
    sysbus.nvic WriteDoubleWord 0xD10 0x10 true
    # RTC1 must be counting for the OLED power-on time polls (get_time_rtc1)
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x40011000 1
"""
runMacro $reset
cpu PerformanceInMips 1000
# AIN0 is the battery sense (GAIN=1, internal 0.6 V reference, 10-bit). The
# firmware uses the raw sample unadapted: 0.39 V reads as a flat battery and the
# boot stops at the low-battery screen; 0.50 V boots the full application.
sysbus.saadc SetInputVoltage 0 0.50
